  "id": "COMPOUND:1169 - DISEASE:1932",
  "verbalization": "Desflurane, a volatile inhalational anesthetic, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Macrostomia through its interaction with the coiled-coil domain containing 33 (CCD33) protein. This protein is a key mediator in multiple pathological conditions, including Hypophosphatemic rickets, Melanoma-Pancreatic cancer syndrome, and Macrostomia itself. The evidence suggests that desflurane affects CCD33, which in turn leads to the development of Macrostomia. The consistent association across three paths—each linking desflurane to CCD33 and then to Macrostomia—indicates a potential mechanistic pathway where desflurane may modulate CCD33 activity, contributing to the manifestation of Macrostomia. The observed scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct causal link. The involvement of CCD33 in multiple disease states highlights the importance of this protein in cellular processes, and the role of desflurane in influencing its function may offer a novel therapeutic approach for conditions associated with Macrostomia.",
